# Crank Project

This repository is a Go backend service generated by `crank`.

## Detecting a Crank project

A project is a Crank-generated project if it has a `.crank.yaml` file at the project root.

Always check for `.crank.yaml` before deciding how to build, test, run, scaffold, migrate, or add features.

If `.crank.yaml` is present:

- Treat the repository as a Crank project.
- Use the system-installed `crank` CLI for supported tasks.
- Read `.crank.yaml` to determine the project name, module path, and enabled features.
- Do not assume every Crank feature is enabled.
- Do not use `./crank`.

If `.crank.yaml` is not present:

- Do not assume the project is managed by Crank.
- Do not use Crank commands unless the user explicitly asks you to.

## Crank CLI usage

Use the system-installed `crank` binary. Do not use a local `./crank` binary.

When commands are run from the project root:

```bash
crank run
crank build
crank test
crank gofmt
crank vet
crank tidy
crank swag
crank migrate up
crank seed up
crank seed generate
```

When commands are run from outside the project root, pass `--project`:

```bash
crank test --project /path/to/project
crank run --project /path/to/project
crank migrate up --project /path/to/project
crank seed up --project /path/to/project
crank seed generate --project /path/to/project
```

If the `crank` command is missing, check with:

```bash
command -v crank
```

If it is unavailable, tell the user that the Crank CLI must be installed. Do not assume a local project binary exists.

## Feature-aware behavior

Read `.crank.yaml` to determine enabled features.

Feature behavior:

| Feature | What exists |
|---|---|
| `base` | Always present — DDD layout, config, logging, validator |
| `gorm` | GORM is the ORM; repos live under `internal/adapters/persistence/gorm/` |
| `bun` | Bun is the ORM; repos live under `internal/adapters/persistence/bun/` |
| `auth` | JWT auth at `internal/adapters/auth/jwt/`, password hashing at `pkg/crypto/`, token denylist in GORM adapter, `/auth/*` endpoints |
| `redis` | Redis cache adapter at `internal/adapters/cache/redis/`, Cache port at `internal/ports/cache.go` |
| `mongodb` | MongoDB client at `internal/adapters/persistence/mongodb/` |
| `qdrant` | Qdrant port at `internal/ports/qdrant.go`, gRPC + HTTP clients at `internal/adapters/persistence/qdrant/` |
| `temporal` | Workflows/activities at `internal/adapters/temporal/`, worker at `cmd/worker/main.go` |
| `otel` | OpenTelemetry tracing at `internal/adapters/telemetry/` |
| `outbox` | Transactional outbox at `internal/adapters/outbox/`, outbox_events table, GORM/Bun UoW with TxRepositories |
| `crypto` | AES-256-GCM cipher at `pkg/crypto/`, Cipher port at `internal/ports/cipher.go` |
| `audit` | Audit trail at `internal/adapters/audit/`, audit_events table, `/api/v1/audit/events` endpoint |

Do not assume all features exist. Check `.crank.yaml` first.

## Architecture conventions

### Project layout

```
cmd/server/main.go           — composition root, DDD wiring
internal/
  domain/{aggregate}/        — aggregates, events, repository ports, errors
  application/{aggregate}/   — command/query handlers, CQRS
  adapters/http/web/v1/      — Echo HTTP handlers (versioned at /api/v1)
  adapters/http/web/api/     — api.Error envelope
  adapters/persistence/      — GORM/Bun repos (row DTO pattern, never scan into aggregate)
  ports/                     — cross-cutting interfaces
  application/uow/           — UnitOfWork + TxRepositories port
configs/                     — YAML config (non-secrets)
pkg/                         — shared packages (logging, crypto)
```

### ID type

All aggregates use `uuid.UUID` from `github.com/google/uuid`. Commands carry `ID string` which is parsed to `uuid.UUID` in the command handler. Generates a new UUID when empty on create.

### Row DTO pattern

Persistence adapters use a private `{name}Row` struct with GORM/Bun tags and `toAggregate()`/`rowFromAggregate()` conversion functions. Domain aggregates have no ORM tags. Constructors (`NewAggregate()`) validate invariants; `Rehydrate()` bypasses validation for persistence round-trips.

### Unit of Work

Writes go through `uow.SaveAndPublish(ctx, func(ctx, repos TxRepositories) error { ... }, events)`. The save closure receives a `TxRepositories` that hands out transaction-scoped repositories. Command handlers never import persistence adapters or `*gorm.DB`.

With the `outbox` feature, the UoW runs in a GORM/Bun transaction and appends outbox rows atomically. Without outbox, it uses an in-memory UoW that is non-transactional.

### Handlers

HTTP handlers live in `package v1` under `internal/adapters/http/web/v1/`. Routes mount at `e.Group("/api/v1")`. Self-scoped endpoints (like users) verify `user_id == c.Param("id")`. All error responses use `api.Error` from `internal/adapters/http/web/api/`.

### Authentication

JWT token service at `internal/adapters/auth/jwt/`. Middleware at `internal/adapters/http/web/middleware/auth.go` stores `user_id` in Echo context. Refresh tokens are denylisted on logout via `ports.TokenDenylist` (GORM-backed).

## Code generation

Prefer Crank generators for new resources.

```bash
crank make model Order customer:string total:float
crank make handler Product title:string price:float
crank make scaffold Invoice number:string amount:float
crank make scaffold Invoice number:string --tests
crank make repository Ticket
crank make service Cart
crank make migration create_orders
crank seed generate Order --count 20
```

For Temporal projects:

```bash
crank make workflow OrderFulfillment order_id:uuid
crank make activity ChargeCard amount:float --tests
```

When running from outside the project root, add `--project /path/to/project`.

Generated handlers auto-wire into `internal/adapters/http/web/v1/routes.go`. Generated aggregates auto-wire into `TxRepositories` interfaces.

## Adding features

Use Crank to add supported features:

```bash
crank add redis
crank add mongodb
crank add temporal
crank add audit
```

When adding features, preserve user edits. Crank uses marker-based injection (`// crank:config-fields`, `# crank:config-section`, etc.) for config and wiring.

## Validation workflow

After making code changes, prefer:

```bash
crank gofmt
crank test
crank vet
```

Run the narrowest relevant Go test first, then broader validation.

## Makefile fallback

Crank owns common dev commands. Unknown `crank <command>` names delegate to project-specific Makefile targets.

```bash
crank clean
crank custom-target key=value
```

Native Crank commands always take precedence over Makefile targets.
